2. **Renderer** — `app/tools/pieces/t6_plateau.py`: mirror-tiled port
   `grass1` (plus signed two-octave olive gain), one 1024² native pass → one
   Lanczos downsample to 512². The rim is a periodic multi-octave Fourier curve
   with two gully tongues and two wall bulges; the wall uses stretched `rock1`
   high-pass flutes with strong x-warp, organic amplitude patches, four dark
   recess slits, vertical waviness, a lit-top→shadow-foot palette ramp, a
   contact shadow under the grass rim, an AO collar above it and foot AO. One
   right-edge sector blends the wall continuously into a walkable grass slope.
   A 64² port-height model (flat top 2.964, 2-tile steep lip, 6-tile walkable
   ramp) supplies the geometry metrics.
   `terrain_piece_render.py` is imported READ-ONLY (`_png`, `mirror_tileable`,
   `wrap_crop`, `adjust_bcs`, comparison primitives); it is never edited.
3. **Acceptance** — every criterion of `docs/T6_WAVE_PLAN.md` T6-T07,
