### Why criterion 5 is recorded as FAIL and not argued away

The literal spec asks for ≥4 of 8 luminance bins ≥3% *and* L std ≤10. An
independent probe of the donor's own clean plateau crop gave **2 bins** at
std 8.06 — the two halves of that criterion conflict for a near-planar
surface. I keep the literal FAIL (38 olive patch clusters are reported
separately) and raise the conflict as an open question rather than redefining
the gate.

## 4. Visual judgement — PASS (cautious), compare sheet read back

I read both written PNGs (`t6_plateau.png` alone and
`t6_plateau_compare.png` beside donor crop C and the donor rim zoom). The port
side shows a near-planar olive grass top, a winding rock/earth rim of strongly
variable thickness, dark recess slits, flutes whose spacing and strength vary
between smooth and deeply striated sections, a lit upper edge grading into a
shadowed foot, a soft AO collar on the grass above the rim, a contact shadow
directly under it, and a gentle grassy ramp where the wall tapers out at the
right edge. There is **no black contour, no round green dome, no regular
checker/comb pattern, and no absent contact shadow** — the three failure modes
the coordinator flagged from T05 are absent. Against the donor rim zoom the
wall is still somewhat cleaner and less deeply weathered, and the piece lacks
trees and the donor's full branching gully network; those are combo/whole-map
concerns, not a single-tile defect. Under "metrics never override visual
review" I record a **cautious PASS** and invite the parent spot-check.

### Iterations (kept / reverted)

* v1 rendered a near-constant-width ribbon with a uniform vertical comb and a
  rectangular green gap → rejected visually (same class as T05's FAIL).
* v2 added variable thickness, notches, warp, recesses and AO → kept.
* v3 added a diagonal tributary gully; on reading the PNG it appeared as a
  clean triangular scratch → **reverted** (T05 lesson: do not keep a degrading
  iteration to chase a metric).
* v4 replaced periodic flute amplitude with organic value noise and retuned
  the lit/shadow palette to the canonical hexes → kept (final).

